window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"locke","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Locke","Locke","Zaahen","Skill","Zaahen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your bully window: Q Ritual Nails marks plus Silver Stake on-hits tax his half-built melee kit, and E Ashen Pursuit resets keep you a step outside his answer - chip him every wave."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"His spike: the W stab pulls you in from 850 range and his E dash follows on an 8-10s cooldown - stop auto-trading, hold E as an escape, and never get pulled with W half-committed."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ult chicken: Purgatory's grounding denies his E dash, so drop it as he steps up - but his passive revives him at full Determination, so a totem spent on the execute can kill nothing."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His bruiser item beats your component: W Ominous Return drain out-lasts your one W Soul Ignition window, so poke from range and only burst when his E is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Nail marks layered before every W commit","E Ashen Pursuit saved to escape his E dive","His R baited before your totem gamble"],"foe":["Q Darkin Glaive chip stacking between waves","E Golden Onslaught the moment your E is down","Extended fights his Q and R healing carry"]},"early":"Level 1 is honest farming - your nails sting but nothing forces a real trade yet. Levels 2-3 belong to you: Q Ritual Nails marks plus Silver Stake on-hits bleed a melee kit that has no full combo, and E Ashen Pursuit resets mean his early E Golden Onslaught never catches the real you - chip relentlessly.","mid":"At 4-5 the momentum flips: his Q Darkin Glaive poke taxes you at your own game and E Golden Onslaught bursts your thin health pool, so shorten trades and respect his rotation. Level 6 is a genuine coin-flip - your R Purgatory totem executes an over-committed Zaahen, but his R Final Retribution lockdown deletes a Locke caught mid-combo - whoever spends their ultimate second wins.","late":"His first bruiser item out-lasts your burst window - his Q and R both heal him, and tank stats grind through your one W Soul Ignition rotation - so give that stretch respect. Late settles into a skill stalemate: your totem threshold executes any over-extension, but his passive revive can undo it, so buy Grievous Wounds, pick him off at range and never brawl.","whys":["Level 1 is even farm - your nails sting him but nothing forces a real trade yet.","Level 2 is yours: Q Ritual Nails poke and Silver Stake on-hits tax a melee kit with no full combo.","Level 3 stays yours - layered marks set up W Soul Ignition burst while E Ashen Pursuit resets keep you out of reach.","At 4-5 he spikes: his W pull drags you in from 850 range and the E dash burst punishes your squishy frame.","Level 6 is even - your R Purgatory totem against his R Final Retribution lockdown comes down to who commits first.","On his first bruiser item his Q and R self-healing out-lasts your single burst window.","Late settles to skill - your growing execute threshold picks off his over-extensions, but his rotation wins straight duels."]});

